ANSWER: {"completedSection": "We conduct quarterly customer satisfaction surveys, supplemented by monthly feedback from sales and support teams, and annual formal surveys. Results are analyzed using statistical methods to identify trends and significant changes. Action triggers include a decline in satisfaction scores below a predetermined threshold, recurring negative feedback on specific issues, or a significant drop in repeat business. Trends are tracked over time to assess the effectiveness of implemented improvements. Results are communicated to all employees through monthly meetings and are reviewed in quarterly management reviews.

References: ISO 9001:2015, Clause 9.1.2; Voice of the Customer (VoC) best practices; Statistical Process Control (SPC) methods.

ClauseAlignment": "This procedure aligns with ISO 9001:2015 Clause 9.1.2 by ensuring regular monitoring of customer satisfaction through multiple data sources, employing systematic analysis, setting clear action triggers, tracking trends, and ensuring effective communication of results to relevant stakeholders."}
